<section class="section" id="why">
  <div class="wrap why">
    <div class="why__copy">
      <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__dot"></span>Why it exists</p>
      <h2 class="display">Your eyes work hard for you. Screens make them work worse.</h2>
      <p>
        During focused computer use, people blink far less often than they do
        in conversation. That drop is a well-known driver of digital eye strain:
        dryness, grit, fatigue, and blurred vision.
      </p>
      <p>
        The problem is not that you “forget to care.” It is that attention
        narrows, the face stills, and blinking becomes sparse and uneven, and
        you rarely notice until the eyes already hurt.
      </p>
      <p>
        EyesRhythm’s motivation is simple: give the eyes a rhythm they can keep,
        for as long as the work needs to last. Maximize your healthy desk ORI,
        use practice daily, it helps to build muscle memory. The app does not
        lecture. It watches, scores, and, if you ask it to, gently nudges.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        It is a wellness companion, not a medical device. It is not intended to
        diagnose, treat, or prevent disease. Persistent discomfort or a change
        in vision belongs with a licensed eye-care professional.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="why__photo">
      <img
        src="/images/desk.jpg"
        alt="A quiet oak desk with a small plant, a cup of tea, and a linen notebook in morning light."
        width="1280"
        height="720"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Built for desk hours. A small companion that stays out of the way of
        the work.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

